FUN_1000_5214: install the FAR reloc/method-vector section si=0x2f0 (dropped BX/SI on the DGROUP:0x12 service).

asm 0x15214: xor bx,bx ; mov si,0x2f0 ; lcall [DGROUP:0x12] ; lret.  DGROUP:0x12 = the reloc service
FUN_0000_f842 (verified: 0xf69:0x1b2 = linear 0xf842).  f842's caller BX is IGNORED for near/far selection:
f842 calls f7c3 which loads BX from the table segment DGROUP:0x74 (0x3352) and loops until it is nonzero;
the applier itself is selected by the DGROUP service SLOT (0x0a/0x0e = near f7ef/f81d; 0x12/0x16 = FAR
f842/f860).  f842 (asm 0xf84d..): `lods ax` reads a leading SEG word (cx), then for each (off,val) pair
writes DGROUP[off]=val and DGROUP[off+2]=seg until off==0 -- i.e. the is_far=1 semantics of
fist_apply_reloc_section.  The __allregs indirect service call `(*DAT_1000_c012)()` dropped the BX/SI
register args, so f842 ran with garbage and a stack-garbage section pointer -> SIGSEGV; and the engine's
f7c3/f842 are inert anyway (Ghidra dropped their x86 string-op DS/ES segment bases).  Install the section
faithfully from the game's own in-image relocation table (seg 0x3352:si; base-0 => identity) via the
loader-role shim fist_apply_reloc_section(0x2f0, is_far=1), exactly as patch 022 does at 4b16 for si=0x274.
This is the engine's own install site (app_entry stage), so the timing is correct.  (An earlier revision
passed is_far=0 -- WRONG: the seg word was misread as an off, so DGROUP:0x468..0x4ec were never installed
and DGROUP:0xf69/0x5bbe got garbage; verified by gdb the far vectors were 0 with is_far=0 and correct
0x5bbe:0xf69 with is_far=1.)
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
